    "overall_comment": "The translation preserves the 99-line dialogue structure, speaker attribution, and most of the scientific content well. However, it contains serious isolated-language corruptions: Chinese characters appear inside a Korean clause (\"그 답은确立되는데\"), and Persian text is attached to Korean (\"멈춰라گوید\"). There are also malformed backchannels (\"어요?\"), several unnatural or calqued Korean constructions, and a substantive conditional reversal in the rendering of “Unless you're clever,” which becomes effectively “unless you are not clever.” The wording for “implacable” as “불가역적인” is also a poor semantic choice. These issues make the Korean read noticeably less natural and require revision despite generally solid line alignment and technical coverage."
